 "observations": [
  "The page number «243» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it. At the foot, the signature «31*» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. Two columns divided by a vertical rule, as on pp. [241]-242 (JP2 0275-0276), transcribed column by column: the left column L01-L51, the right L52-L98; the letter heads «G.» (L01), «H.» (L21), «I.» (L61) and «J.» (L86) in bold, centred in their columns, the last three each after a blank line; each entry begins at the edge of its column, its further lines indented.",
  "The semicolons of L15, L33, L37, L47, L65 and L87 and the colon of L38 stand after a thin space (7-12 px); written with a space. Dashes: «60—66» (L11) 27 px, «9—14» and «15—18» (L46-L47) 36-37 px, «17—19» (L13) 36 px in three pieces, «6—9» (L47) 32 px; «69‐‐71» (L11) is made up of two short dashes (17 and 13 px with a gap of 2 px), here written as two hyphens (U+2010). L15: «(fem).» with the point after the parenthesis, as printed. L52: «Loos», the older spelling of «Los».",
  "Checked against the text, for example: «Gavzehar» on p. 9 (JP2 0041), «Gedval» in the titles of Tab. 60-66 and 69-71 (pp. 174-185), «Genubium» and «genubia» on p. 29 (JP2 0061), «Harket elscems» in Tab. 61 (p. 175, JP2 0207), «Helhacib» on p. XXII and p. 20 (JP2 0026, 0052), «Hemeli» on pp. 13 and 16, «Hormi» on p. XXII and in Tab. 33 and 36, «Idhnascer» in the title of Tab. 79 (p. 194, JP2 0226), «elihtilef» in Tab. 73 (p. 187, JP2 0219), «lilmanshar» on p. 28 (JP2 0060), «submissio» on p. 14 (JP2 0046), «Jumedi elachir» and «Jumedi elule» in Tab. 2 and 3 (pp. 110, 113)."
